  "narrative": {
    "intro": "KBR Services has $484M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. KBR Services has 88 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $5.5M. Obligations fell 42.9% year over year. Year-by-year obligations show prior totals of $1.6B in FY21, $2.1B in FY22, $1.2B in FY23, $1.3B in FY24, and $847M in FY25. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, obligating $472M to KBR Services in FY2026 to date. The Department of State obligated $6.8M and the National Science Foundation obligated $5M. Facilities Support Services is the largest market for KBR Services with $445M in obligations this year. Additional markets include Commercial and Industrial Machinery and Equipment Repair and Maintenance at $23.5M, Engineering Services at $7.8M, Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $6.6M, Hotels (except Casino Hotels) and Motels at $725K, and Postal Service at $239K. These figures are partial, fiscal year to date totals.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has KBR Services' federal business changed year over year?",
        "body": "KBR Services obligated $484M in FY2026 to date. Obligations fell 42.9% year over year. Prior fiscal years show $1.6B in FY21, $2.1B in FY22, $1.2B in FY23, $1.3B in FY24, and $847M in FY25. These totals show higher obligations in earlier years compared with the current fiscal year to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are KBR Services' top government customers and markets?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $472M in FY2026 to date. The Department of State obligated $6.8M and the National Science Foundation obligated $5M. Facilities Support Services is the top market at $445M, followed by Commercial and Industrial Machinery and Equipment Repair and Maintenance at $23.5M and Engineering Services at $7.8M. Other markets include Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $6.6M, Hotels (except Casino Hotels) and Motels at $725K, and Postal Service at $239K."
      }
    ]
